# 🌲 The Tortoise & The Hare — Midnight Forest (Stage 4) 🏃‍♂️🐢

A high-performance, low-level 3D runner game built from scratch using **native WebGL2** and vanilla JavaScript. This project replicates the classic fable with an interactive, mechanics-driven twist, running at a locked **60 FPS** without a single external engine, library, or dependency.

![WebGL2](https://img.shields.io/badge/Graphics-WebGL2-blue?style=flat-square)
![Math](https://img.shields.io/badge/Matrix%20Math-Custom%20Mat4-orange?style=flat-square)
![Dependencies](https://img.shields.io/badge/Dependencies-None%20(Vanilla)-green?style=flat-square)

---

## 🕹️ Live Architecture Overview

The codebase is engineered around deterministic state machine synchronization, handling physics interpolation and real-time GPU matrix updates within a tight rendering context loop.

### 🎮 Dual-Character Playstyles
* **The Hare (Speed & Agility):** High acceleration and exponential velocity spikes (`SHIFT` key Comeback Boost) paired with a high-friction drag index.
* **The Tortoise (Steady & Resilient):** Low base velocity but complete obstacle immunity via a custom 2-second shell shield dynamic (`SHIFT` key). Includes an integrated **Fable AI mechanic** that forces the opponent Hare to take tactical naps if it gets too far ahead.

---

## 🛠️ Technical Architecture & Features

This project serves as a comprehensive exploration of low-level graphics pipeline engineering:

### 📐 Linear Algebra Engine (`mat4.js`)
* **Zero Dependencies:** Implements a custom, column-major 4x4 matrix library mapping directly to standard OpenGL conventions.
* Handles complex affine transformations including look-at camera matrices, symmetric perspective projections, scaling, translating, and compounding arbitrary-axis rotations.

### 🎨 Custom Fragment Shader Pipelines (`main.js`)
Driven by an integer mode uniform identifier mapping to individual render sub-passes:
* **Mode 1 (Organic Terrain Optimization):** Generates structural grass and soil displacement variations utilizing a custom **two-octave value noise algorithms** calculated in world-space coordinates (`xz` plane).
* **Mode 2 (Procedural Sky Box Pre-pass):** Generates a dynamic starfield using a per-cell pseudo-random hash (`hash21`), modulating star size and running a time-dependent sine wave function to control real-time twinkling.
* **Distance Fog Engine:** Implements a **quadratic distance attenuation fog pipeline** covering a $18.0 \to 55.0$ world-unit depth span, seamlessly eliminating asset popping at the horizon boundary.

### 💾 Performance-First Asset Data Maps (`track.js`)
* Tracks the race map layouts across an authoritative 160-row configuration grid matrix.
* Calculates real-time custom 3D bounding box collision detection patterns (AABB XZ) to process frame-by-frame asset interaction variables without lagging code performance loops.

---

## ⌨️ Control Schematics

| Key | Action | Engine Mechanics |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `W` / `S` | Accelerate / Brake | Linearly updates velocity arrays within safe character constants. |
| `A` / `D` or `←` / `→` | Lane Switch | Triggers a smooth geometric lane shift interpolation sequence. |
| `Spacebar` | Jump | Applies instantaneous vertical impulse mapping to gravity vector drops. |
| `Shift` | Special Ability | Triggers exponential acceleration decay or active obstacle shielding. |
| `R` | System Restart | Resets clock, scores, track positions, and clears animation contexts. |

